@startuml activity-quality-gate
!include style.iuml
title The quality gate: what runs before every commit (quality-gate.sh)

start
:Choose a target: backend, db, workflows, ai, mobile,
admin-web, fhir, tls, docs, secrets, or all;
note right
  One target runs its own steps; "all" runs
  every target one after another. In CI each
  target is a separate job, run in parallel.
end note
fork
  :**backend**
  Prettier, ESLint, TypeScript
  Prisma validate
  unit tests, end-to-end tests
  OpenAPI, FHIR definitions and
  access matrix up to date
  build, npm audit (high);
fork again
  :**db**
  migrations applied
  all tests with PostgreSQL, MongoDB,
  MinIO (coverage ≥ 80 %);
fork again
  :**ai**
  ruff format and lint, mypy
  pytest (coverage ≥ 80 %)
  pip-audit;
fork again
  :**mobile**
  dart format, flutter analyze
  flutter test (line coverage ≥ 80 %)
  debug APK build
  package audit (OSV);
fork again
  :**admin-web**
  format, oxlint, typecheck
  Vitest (coverage ≥ 80 %)
  build, npm audit;
fork again
  :**docs, secrets, fhir, tls, workflows**
  links resolve; manual pictures current
  gitleaks (history and staged)
  HL7 FHIR validator; TLS 1.3 at nginx
  six workflows on the live system;
end fork
if (Any step failed?) then (yes)
  :QUALITY GATE FAILED: names the steps;
  :Fix, then run the gate again;
  stop
else (no)
  :QUALITY GATE PASSED;
  :Commit and push. GitHub Actions
  runs the same gate in 8 jobs;
  stop
endif
@enduml
